### Curl example: upload `resume.pdf` to the backend
### Run in a terminal:
curl -v -F "file=@./resume.pdf" http://localhost:8081/api/resume/upload

### VS Code REST Client example (multipart with file contents)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/resume/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="resume.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./resume.pdf
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--

### Match resume to job description (cURL)
curl -v -F "resume=@./resume.pdf" -F "job=@./job.txt" http://localhost:8081/api/resume/match

### REST Client example (match)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/resume/match
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="resume"; filename="resume.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./resume.pdf
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="job"; filename="job.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./job.txt
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--